 ['Fix money leaks','Keep the trip and the price in balance.','Review actual billed price and any unpaid jobs.','Reach people next to current work, not distant cheap jobs.','Quote deep initial cleanup as a separate honest charge.','Record collected gross revenue and route hours.'],
 ['Twenty-eight-stop checkpoint','Build seven average visits each workday.','Count actual weekly stops, not names in a lead list.','Focus one day with fewer than seven visits.','Ask satisfied customers for local introductions.','Compare paid visits to the twenty-eight-stop target.'],
 ['Fill the small gaps','Use the map to make a faster route.','Mark streets with one or two empty openings.','Share that specific day with people nearby.','Move only willing customers if a route change helps.','Measure miles and time per visit.'],
 ['Make referrals routine','Ask after service that earns trust.','Set a reminder to ask after a clean visit.','Ask one customer for an introduction to a neighbor.','Send a personal thanks to each referring customer.','Count introductions and paid weekly starts.'],
 ['Keep people who join','Fix repeat complaints before buying more leads.','List cancellations and reasons from this month.','Check missed visits, gate problems and billing questions.','Call a customer with an open service problem.','Choose one preventable reason to fix next week.'],
 ['Thirty-four-stop checkpoint','Protect reliable service as routes fill.','Check the schedule against time available.','Work near the emptiest real route day.','Confirm payment setup for new weekly customers.','Compare actual weekly stops to the thirty-four-stop target.'],
 ['Go deeper, not wider','Finish a neighborhood before chasing the whole city.','Pick one dense area with remaining openings.','Make permitted contact in that area.','Follow up leads from the same streets.','Compare paid starts per area, not just message likes.'],
 ['Make the next opening clear','Give a true reason to act now.','Count open slots for each workday.','Tell local leads the actual day you can serve.','Use the signup link when someone agrees to start.','Count accepted offers, not clicks alone.'],
 ['Close the warm list','Do not pay for attention while quotes sit open.','Find quoted leads who asked for more time.','Reply to fresh neighborhood interest.','Send the final polite check-in when it is due.','Close lost leads with a reason and move on.'],
 ['Keep the four days balanced','Protect the owner from a long, scattered week.','Count stops and route hours Monday through Thursday.','Seek homes near the emptiest day.','Confirm route days before taking payment.','Record which day needs help next week.'],
 ['Measure the return on work','Know where the money and time go.','Update collected sales and hours worked.','Use only outreach that creates paid starts nearby.','Fix unpaid balances or a recurring service issue.','Review gross per route hour and marketing cash left.'],
 ['Forty-stop checkpoint','Fill four routes without losing the service standard.','Count forty real weekly appointments by weekday.','Fill remaining nearby openings if they exist.','Thank customers and ask for genuine introductions.','Compare reality with the forty-stop goal; keep your best routine.']
